     ]\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"topic_id\\\": \\\"topic-tradeoff-aware-compiler-strategies\\\",\n      \\\"title\\\": \\\"Tradeoff-aware compiler strategies and empirical validation\\\",\n      \\\"structure_type\\\": \\\"wiki\\\",\n      \\\"sections\\\": [\n        \\\"The sources share a view of compiler optimization as a tradeoff problem whose success must be measured rather than assumed.\\\",\n        \\\"Profile-based classic optimizations are presented as complements to conventional optimization, with reported speedups but also measured executable-size growth and separate profiling versus measurement inputs.\\\",\n        \\\"Machine-learning compilation emphasizes empirically trained decisions, but also highlights context dependence, such as thread coarsening improving some performance factors while hurting parallelism or register pressure on particular hardware.\\\",\n        \\\"Distributed quantum compilation compares data-qubit swapping and entanglement swapping under topology and resource constraints, using analytical bounds and medium-size circuit experiments to validate strategy choices.\\\",\n        \\\"A synthesis page could organize compiler strategies by the costs they trade off: runtime versus code size, training-data cost versus prediction quality, and communication depth versus Bell-pair or qubit-resource consumption.\\\"\n      ],\n      \\\"claim_ids\\\": [\n        \\\"claim-profile-based-classic-optimizations-are-intended-to-complement-conventional-opti--6bcefbcf9607\\\",\n        \\\"claim-on-the-benchmark-suite-profile-based-super-block-optimizations-averaged-a-1-15-s--e5d7486c0e56\\\",\n        \\\"claim-the-profile-based-transformations-controlled-executable-size-growth-averaging-1--5bacab4b8a28\\\",\n        \\\"claim-the-experiments-used-separate-profiling-inputs-and-performance-measurement-input--ee5ac2fa5a94\\\",\n        \\\"claim-the-implementation-cost-of-profile-based-classic-optimization-was-modest-relativ--062df22ec16c\\\",\